# Dithered wallpaper, same as the adrianlam.sh dark-mode background (static
# version). Lives in the dark theme only: dark text from linear-light would be
# unreadable on it. The window stays opaque, so this image is exactly what
# shows. Baked, not a custom-shader: a shader would dither the text too and
# costs GPU. Pre-baked from ~/Pictures/wallpaper.jpg, since Ghostty can't do this:
#   1. Dusk grade, blur 6 (site uses 2; softer here), 57% mix toward #17181d.
#   2. Ordered dither, Bayer 4x4, strength 1.0, 4 levels spanning #17181d to
#      +66 per channel. 2pt pixels: dithered at 756px, then nearest-neighbor 4x
#      to 3024px so each pixel is a crisp 4x4 block on Retina.
#   3. Recolored to match the site: everything neutral gray except warm
#      (amber) dots, which take the site accent #ff6719 at the same luma, then
#      65% saturation (muted rust), 85% then 60% brightness.
#   4. Ghostty only: whole image at 85% brightness and 60% saturation, a bit
#      darker and more muted than the site.
#      Darkest tone #0e0e0e.
# Text contrast, worst 1% (4x4-block blend): fg 14.3:1, dim gray (palette 8)
# 3.3:1 (3.6:1 median; plain bg is 3.3:1).
background-image = ~/Pictures/wallpaper-ghostty.png
background-image-opacity = 1
background-image-fit = cover
